  National Institutes ... +1
  The Sequence of an Explosion
  • Radial Expansion: The chemical reaction moves
  outward from the center. It forms a supersonic
  shock front and expanding gas bubble.
  • Blunt Impact: The expanding shock wave and
  high-pressure blast wind smash into nearby
  surfaces. This transfers massive kinetic energy
  and causes physical trauma or structural
  deformation.
  National Institutes ... +1
  • Heave and Drag: Following the initial high-
  pressure blow, the expanding gases push
  materials away or create a vacuum effect ("blast
  wind") that pulls debris back
